# Agent scratch: worktrees and session state, never part of the tree.
.claude/
# No trailing slash on purpose. A pattern that ends in `/` matches only
# DIRECTORIES, so a symlink named `target` — which is how a worktree borrows
# another worktree's build output — sails straight past it and turns up as an
# untracked path next to 300 MB of things it points at. Slice C2, 2026-08-21.
target
*.app/

# The spike's local copy of the pinned gpui fork. Never committed; the fork
# change it carried is now a real commit (8521fc1, see eave-app/Cargo.toml)
# and `spike/gpui-bgra-surface.patch` has been retired. No trailing slash,
# for the reason given above — this is one of the two paths that bit us.
spike/zed-fork

# A derived app icon, if anything ever writes one into the source tree.
# Nothing does today: `scripts/bundle-app.sh` synthesises the iconset inside
# the bundle it is assembling and never touches `crates/`. Kept as a guard,
# because the script that DID write here (`package-web.sh`, Slice C1) was
# deleted in C3 and a stray .icns is not worth a commit.
crates/eave-app/resources/mac/eave.icns
